# Where the built app looks for the API.
#
# Committed on purpose. Leaving it to a dashboard variable is how this broke
# twice: once set to the bare host, so every call landed on /auth/... instead of
# /api/auth/... and returned 404, and once deleted in favour of a same-origin
# /api proxy that had not actually deployed, so every call 404'd at the CDN and
# never reached the backend at all. A value in the repository is a value that
# deploys with the code that expects it.
#
# This is an absolute URL, so the site and the API are different origins and the
# refresh cookie has to be allowed across them. The backend needs:
#
#   REFRESH_COOKIE_SAMESITE=None
#   CORS_ALLOWED_ORIGINS=https://admissionportal.gabstep.com
#
# Both are already set on Render. `None` is required because a browser will not
# send a `Lax` cookie from one host to another, and the session would be lost on
# every reload.
#
# To move to same-origin later, which is tidier and allows `Lax`: add a rewrite
# on the frontend host sending /api to the backend, confirm it answers, and only
# then change this to /api. Confirm first. That order matters.
#
# A dashboard variable of the same name still wins over this file, so clear it
# there if it is set.
VITE_API_URL=https://gabstep-backend.onrender.com/api
